An open note to the Dev Team and anybody else who might be interested
(since I'm in a manic, self-centered, egotistical phase right now,
please forgive what I am about to say - I'm not in my right mind):

WHERE THE H-E-DOUBLE-HOCKEY-STICKS IS VERSION 3.1?

It has now been one year and six months since the last patch level of
verion 3.0 was released, and what, four years (?) since version 3.0 was
first released!  Where is this long promised, long "close-to-finished-
but-we-can't-tell-you-when-we're-going-to-release-it-because-it's-a-
secret" version of Nethack?

I seem to recall a message from a Dev Team member at one point (I can't
for the life of me remember who it was or even if it was e-mail or on
the net) intimating that the daily exchange of information between the
Dev Team members was in excess of 1 megabyte.  If this were the case,
the Dev Team should have been able to either A) expand the game by
3000%, making it the first truly artificially intelligent computer game,
B) expand the documentation to the size of the Encyclopedia Britannica,
or C) send an *awful* lot of notes back and forth to the effect of 
"Wouldn't it be cool if we could do X?," and "Yeah it would, can you
program that?," and "No, can you?"

Come on guys!  HAVE YOU ALL DIED?!?!?

WE WANT NETHACK 3.1!  At the very least, I'd like some kind of message
posted "officially" by the Dev Team telling us what is taking so 
darned long, and giving us at least an *idea* of when we can expect
version 3.1!  (Next month?  Next year?  Next century?)

Anyways, my wife is bodily wrestling me off my soapbox and to the ground
right now, muttering something about "Stupid obnoxious nethack addict"
and "Get the Dev Team mad and I won't get *my* next fix," so I'll end
this message while I still can.

PLEASE, tell us something?

	  - Paul
